{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:5-3","provision":"BCO 5-3","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"5-3","title":"Section 5-3","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/5-3/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/5-3","current_text":{"html":"<p>The mission church, because of its transitional condition, requires a temporary system of government. Depending on the circumstances and at its own discretion, Presbytery may provide for such government in one of several ways: a. Appoint an evangelist as prescribed in <i>BCO </i>8-6. b. Cooperate with the Session of a particular church in arranging a mother-daughter relationship with a mission church. The Session may then serve as the temporary governing body of the mission church. c. Appoint a <i>BCO</i> 15-1 commission to serve as a temporary Session of the mission church. When a minister of the Presbytery has been approved to serve as pastor of the mission church, he shall be included as a member of the commission and serve as its moderator. The temporary system of government shall record and submit its records to Presbytery for annual review in the same manner as Sessions of particular churches.</p>","text":"The mission church, because of its transitional condition, requires a temporary system of government. Depending on the circumstances and at its own discretion, Presbytery may provide for such government in one of several ways: a. Appoint an evangelist as prescribed in BCO 8-6. b. Cooperate with the Session of a particular church in arranging a mother-daughter relationship with a mission church. The Session may then serve as the temporary governing body of the mission church. c. Appoint a BCO 15-1 commission to serve as a temporary Session of the mission church. When a minister of the Presbytery has been approved to serve as pastor of the mission church, he shall be included as a member of the commission and serve as its moderator. The temporary system of government shall record and submit its records to Presbytery for annual review in the same manner as Sessions of particular churches."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"f8bde72b35f9475713a5751081d525f119bc6b4daf3b43ddc86694065015654b","parent_id":"bco:5","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":30,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:5-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Requirements for Reporting and Reviewing Minutes of a Mission Church","year":2016,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-3--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.md:occ-9970d56cf041","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB found the overture in conflict with BCO 5-3.a because an evangelist, unlike governing bodies, has no minutes to submit under the BCO.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga44_2016__ci02.md"}]},{"id":"bco:5-3--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Bigelow v. North Florida Presbytery","year":2025,"disposition":"granted","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-3--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md:occ-9c6b44ae6746","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":119},"excerpt":"3. \"That the Presbytery transfer oversight of \"Christ Church Beaches\" from the Presbytery established \"provisional session” to the MNA Committee (BCO 5-3c), effective, February 12, 2024, to allow the committee to undertake an assessment of the congregation's o","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["call dissolution","assistant pastor","church planting","mission church","pastoral relationship","discipline without process","mediation commission","BCO 43 complaint","BCO 23-1","congregational vote","provisional session","BCO 5 mission church","dissolution of pastoral call","congregational rights","mediation","nondisclosure agreement","contumacy","BCO 12-5-e session pulpit authority","women preaching","call dissolution procedure","mission church governance"],"case_numbers":["2024-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Kevin Bigelow complained against multiple actions of North Florida Presbytery related to the dissolution of his call as Assistant Pastor of Christ Church East (where he was also serving as planting pastor at Christ Church Beaches). The SJC sustained the complaint in part (22-0-0), finding that Presbytery erred in…"}},{"id":"bco:5-3--case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"the Session of Hope Community Church v. Central Carolina Presbytery","year":2014,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-3--case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md:occ-6adc6d4391e7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["multi-site church","particularization","session authority over time and place of worship","presbytery manual","church planting policy","mission church","presbytery limits on session authority","BCO vs. presbytery rules"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2013-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Hope Community Church’s Session challenged Presbytery’s requirement that a multi-site congregation eventually particularize its second worship site. The SJC sustained the complaint, annulled the requirement, and struck it from the Presbytery Manual because BCO 12-5e specifically entrusts the time and place of worship to the Session, which Presbytery’s general church-enlargement authority could not supersede. The narrow ruling did not resolve broader concerns about multi-site churches or eliminate Presbytery’s review of a second site’s location under BCO 13-9(g)."}},{"id":"bco:5-3--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Smith v. Northeast Presbytery","year":1994,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-3--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md:occ-571b17aea8c0","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":201},"excerpt":"etc. (BCO 5-3, 5-4). One express exception is given to the presbytery in BCO","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["dissolved congregation","presbytery administrative commission","church membership","jurisdiction","complaint procedure","constitutional rights"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1993-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Smith complained that Northeast Presbytery failed to provide pastoral care after dissolving Grace Presbyterian Church. The SJC rejected Presbytery's objections that the complaint lacked supporting reasons or was barred by Smith's protest, held it in order, but denied it on the merits. Distinguishing the pastoral 'power of order' from judicial 'power of jurisdiction,' the SJC ruled that the Constitution neither requires nor permits a presbytery to retain jurisdiction over individual members of a dissolved particular church, and that pastoral care of former members is generally discretionary; on these facts, Presbytery's efforts satisfied any duty."}},{"id":"bco:5-3--overture:ga44_2016:38","reco